Stack:
Linear data structure that follows LIFO.(Last In First Out).

Real life examples:

Stack of plates
browser back button
undo operation in editions

Operations: 
Insert element - push,
Remove top of the stack - pop, 
peek - View top of the stack, 
isEmpty - check if stack is empty, 
size - Number of elements

TOS=size  -> push -> Stack Overflow
TOS==-1   -> pop ->  Stack Underflow

top==size-1 

Queue: It is a linear data structure follows FIFO principle.

Real life example: 
Ticket counter
Printer queue
CPU scheduling
 
Operations:
Enqueue -> Insert at rear
Dequeue -> remove from front
peek -> Front element

 i)Deque: Double ended queue is a linear data structure in which
 insertion and deletion can be performed from both rear and front ends.
 
 Combination of stack and queue.
 
 
 
 ii)Circular queue
 
 
 Expressions: Expressions are ways of writing logical/arithmetical 
 operations using operators like +,/,* etc and operands(values or variables).
 
 Common expressions:
 i)Infix expression
 ii)Prefix Expression(Polish notation)
 iii)Postfix expression(reverse polish notation)
 
 
 example: (Operand operator Operand)
 A+B
 
 A+B*C
 
 A+(B*C) - according to operator precedence
 
 Prefix Expression:(Operator operand Operand) - Operator comes before 
 operands
 +AB
 *AC
 *+ABC
 Evaluation direction: Right -> Left
 
 Postfix Expression:( operand operand Operator)- Operator comes after
 operands
 
 AB+
 AB*
 AB+C*
 
  Evaluation direction: Left -> Right
  
  Postfix expression: 5 3 + 2 *
  
  Stack used for evaluation
  
  Step 1:push 5  stack:[5]
  step 2:push 3  stack:[5,3] 
  step 3:Encountered +  stack:[8] 
  step 4:push 2 stack:[8,2]
  step 5:Encountered * stack:[16] 
  
  Prefix expression: * + 5 3 2
  
  =16
  
  Postfix Evaluation
  
  Monotonic Stack/Queue: It is a special data structure that maintains
  its elements in a specific order.(increasing/decreasing)
  
  [12,34,56,78,89]
 
  push :
  
  while(!stack.isEmpty() && stack.peek()>currentElement)
